NMSEF Display criteria
Display Skill (10 pts)
Judges ask:
Is the work neat and carefully done?
Is the lettering clear?
Are colors strong and suitable?
Is the layout complete, logical, and self-explanatory?
Is the content clearly and logically presented?
Dramatic Value (10 pts)
Judges ask:
Is the display simple and visually balanced?
Does it capture attention?
Does it have impact?
Practical “what to do” for a CS/AI project display
To score well on those points, your board should make the story obvious in under 30 seconds:
Big title + one-sentence research question at the top.
A single pipeline diagram (Canvas → extraction → misconceptions → blueprint → questions → adaptive practice → results).
A methods block: control vs adaptive, time-on-task, metrics.
Results: 2–3 graphs (pre→post gain, repeat-error rate, time-to-mastery).
Example output: one MCQ with a citation + misconception-based distractor explanation (small but visible).
Keep text short; use headings and consistent spacing.